{
  "id": "2026-09-14-documents-oss-fidelity-review",
  "scope": "documents",
  "kind": "review",
  "date": "2026-09-14",
  "question": "Which document conversion laws should DOCX file import, export and Word paste share, and where must fidelity limits be explicit?",
  "model": null,
  "method": "best-api-review/history-v2",
  "trigger": "User selected the documents ledger audit after skipping diff and explicitly requested current OSS research through Best API Review, Research Wiki and Plite Research before choosing the target.",
  "requirements": [
    "Keep detached DOCX import, snapshot export and Word clipboard fitting as distinct current jobs; independent Plate features stay separate.",
    "Word content must not be silently replaced by an unverified stale native sidecar; all export parts must use one captured document.",
    "Preserve canonical authored ownership and existing before/after property facts; expose deliberate review projections and actionable unsupported/lossy conversion results.",
    "Respect installed schema, comments/ranges, media and transfer owners; retain remote resources opt-in, app-owned export styling and lazy file dependencies.",
    "Compare maximum-value deletion, merge/reuse and direct OOXML replacement against current HTML machinery; do not adopt a runtime without complete-operation correctness and scale evidence.",
    "Complete bounded official discovery and exact-source investigation for seven corpus families with explicit evidence gaps; do not treat proprietary engine contracts or preview retention as inspected OSS preservation proof."
  ],
  "evidenceReuse": "Rechecked September 8 DOCX plan: its standalone jobs and optional styling remain justified, while its deliberately unchanged algorithms and historical packed proof do not settle current authored conversion. Reconciled prior no-universal-rich-AST rejection and September 10 authored research. Fetched current html-to-docx, SuperDoc and CKEditor commits without changing their older checkouts; four other source clones match current default branch. All selected upstream file hashes verified. Current Plate source and real callers reread; main executed four partitions and two bug probes; independent worker supplied additional fixture/demo results.",
  "summary": "Pursue a documents design plan. Strongest cuts are unconditional private-sidecar authority and duplicate review schema serialization. Two local public-operation probes confirm silently ignored Word-body edits and mixed export snapshots; 135 unique existing tests pass across main and worker evidence. Direct OOXML adapters are the strongest replacement candidate to compare with a repaired shared HTML path, but the runtime and package-preservation claim are not accepted. Keep paste/file boundaries and canonical authored ownership; make projection, loss and full-document adoption explicit.",
  "verdict": "pursue",
  "previous": null,
  "relation": "initial",
  "alternatives": [
    "Keep/configure: retain detached import, snapshot export, clipboard lifecycle, lazy dependencies and app styling; current configuration cannot fix competing authority or bypassed serializer options.",
    "Delete/merge/inline: remove unconditional sidecar authority and duplicate literal review serialization; compare one file-export result/projection contract; minor catalog/demo cuts require caller reconciliation.",
    "Reuse/move: canonical authored snapshots already own before/after properties; feature codecs own schema; transfer owns fitting; DOCX owns Word encoding; UI owns comment workflow and palette.",
    "Repair HTML: share configured semantic serialization and add exact Word mappings/diagnostics; this remains a comparator and cannot recover facts discarded by import.",
    "Replace file conversion with direct OOXML adapters: strongest breaking candidate for revisions, comment ranges, numbering, relationships and schema properties; library, API, complete-operation scale and adoption proof remain provisional.",
    "Add retained package or OOXML-backed editor: defer unless an actual arbitrary-package editing job justifies its second representation, identity and lifetime; current source comparison does not prove it.",
    "Merge a universal Office/document framework or canonical AST: stop; clipboard fragments, file conversion, CSV, pagination and authored runtime have distinct jobs and owners."
  ],
  "proofLimits": "Main: 123 existing tests in four source-based DOCX partitions plus two bug-observation probes (not correctness acceptance). Worker: 12 additional fixture/demo/selected-roundtrip tests; duplicate 123-test run adds no coverage. No complete slow-suite, current packed-install, browser clipboard, native Word/LibreOffice, performance or arbitrary preservation proof. Seven bounded source corpora, 67 current selected external files; zero upstream tests and zero issue/PR bodies. SuperDoc proprietary v2 engine is an explicit evidence gap; CKEditor proprietary file converters are outside the inspected paste lane. Source-revision manifest tracks fetched object reads independently of unchanged older checkout HEADs. Design, implementation and doctrine/doc repair remain outstanding.",
  "references": [
